<h3 style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:12.0pt;color:#5B9BD5'
lang=3Dnl-BE>Situation</h3>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt' lang=3Dnl-BE>In
signals the items in an experiment need to have a unique name.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt' lang=3Dnl-BE>P=
reparations
sub tables are created uing an external action based on the preparation mas=
ter
table. The table name is the name of the preparation. Lines in a table can =
have
the same name.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt' lang=3Dnl-BE>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt' lang=3Dnl-BE>C=
urrently
when a user trigger the external action to create preparations tables, ther=
e is
no check or warning about duplicated names in the preparation name. However=
 the
table is not created. The users sees that and needs to update the data and
restart the external action whic is a slow process.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt' lang=3Dnl-BE>I=
f there
would be a warning at the strart of the external action, this can be
corrected<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span>early by the users =
and they do
not have to wait too long for this action.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt' lang=3Dnl-BE>U=
sers can
also copy a line in the master table with a prep ID updating the name and t=
hen
we have a master table with 2 prep names but the same prep ID.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt' lang=3Dnl-BE><=
span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0</span></p>

